/T (1.2 Graph Theory in Urban Planning Graph theory, a branch of mathematics established by Leonhard Euler in 1736, provides the fundamental framework for our analyzer. In our context, an urban area is represented as a directed or undirected graph G = \(V, E\), where V is the set of vertices \(locations\) and E is the set of edges \(roads\). )
