/T (Congestion is a major driver of localized pollution. Vehicles in stop-and-go traffic consume significantly more fuel and emit more particulates than those moving at a steady pace. By routing traffic away from bottlenecks, our system helps in flattening the "congestion curve," leading to cleaner air in urban centers. )
/E (Congestion is a major driver of localized pollution. Vehicles in stop-and-go traffic consume significantly more fuel and emit more particulates than those moving at a steady pace. By routing traffic away from bottlenecks, our system helps in flattening the "congestion curve," leading to cleaner air in urban centers. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
