<<
/Title (12.5 Multi-Modal Routing The graph could be expanded to include metro lines and bus routes. The analyzer could then provide "Mixed-Mode" travel plans \(e.g., "Drive to Station A, take the Metro to Station B, then walk to Destination"\).)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1006 0 R
/Next 566 0 R
>>
endobj
819 0 obj
<<
/Title (The "Smart City Traffic & Road Network Analyzer" represents a successful synthesis of classical graph theory and modern urban problem-solving. Through the implementation of Dijkstra's and Tarjan's algorithms in an optimized C++ environment, we have created a tool that provides both immediate routing benefits for individuals and deep structural insights for city administrators.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 566 0 R
/Next 1007 0 R
>>
endobj
820 0 obj
<<
/Title (In conclusion, this analyzer is more than just a piece of software; it is a framework for a more efficient, sustainable, and resilient urban future. It proves that with the right data structures and algorithms, we can navigate the complexities of modern urbanization and ensure that our cities remain engines of progress rather than centers of congestion.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 566 0 R
/Prev 1008 0 R
>>
endobj
