1476 0 obj
<<
/Title (The innovation of this project lies in its dynamic weighting system. Unlike standard digital maps where the primary metric is physical distance, our system recognizes that a road's "cost" is a multi- dimensional variable. A 5-kilometer road might be "cheaper" to traverse than a 2-kilometer road if the latter is clogged with rush-hour traffic. By integrating time-indexed traffic coefficients, we provide a more realistic and actionable routing tool for the modern driver.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1241 0 R
/Prev 1597 0 R
>>
endobj
1477 0 obj
<<
/Title (1.1 Theoretical Background of Smart Cities The concept of a "Smart City" revolves around the integration of Information and Communication Technology \(ICT\) and various physical devices connected to the Internet of Things \(IoT\) network to optimize the efficiency of city operations and services. The primary goal is to improve the quality of life for citizens and the sustainability of urban environments. Smart mobility is a cornerstone of this vision.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1241 0 R
/Next 1598 0 R
>>
endobj
1478 0 obj
<<
