/Title (Traffic congestion is not merely a matter of personal frustration; it is a systemic failure with cascading economic and environmental consequences. In major clusters like the National Capital Region \(NCR\), commuters spend an average of 1.5 to 2 hours in daily transit. This loss of time translates directly into billions of dollars of lost economic productivity annually. Environmentally, idling vehicles contribute significantly to carbon emissions and local air pollution, further degrading the health of the urban population. Traditional traffic management systems, which often rely on fixed-cycle signals or static navigation maps, are increasingly proving inadequate in handling the dynamic and fluid nature of today's city traffic.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1241 0 R
/Prev 1475 0 R
/Next 1597 0 R
>>
endobj
1597 0 obj
<<
/Title (The "Smart City Traffic & Road Network Analyzer" is an initiative designed to bridge the gap between theoretical computer science and urban infrastructure management. By conceptualizing the city as a mathematical graph, we can apply rigorous computational logic to find solutions that human intuition or static maps might overlook. This project treats every major intersection, landmark, or residential hub as a 'Node' and the roads connecting them as 'Weighted Edges'.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1241 0 R
/Prev 1596 0 R
/Next 1476 0 R
>>
